z5m = z3x + SYM_KING_SEEN (tools/bundle.sh z5m zl0 z3x z5l; its sorted sources differ from z3x's by the switch's lines
only). On round 1 the first king rules out each live symmetry whose twin of its start it can sense with no enemy robot
within dist2 8 of it: the enemy king starts on the true twin, and Sym otherwise eliminates only by walls and mines.

Evidence (z3x's 144 cached replica games, 98 distinct game-sides; scratch twin1.py): on 21 game-sides a wrong twin of
our start lies within the king's dist2 25 at round 1 (keepout, dirtpassageway, FreeTheCheese, Stash, cheesebottles,
streetsofnewyork, corridorofdoomanddespair and uneasy_alliance in both seats; thunderdome A and B, knifefight A and B,
tiny B). firstSym() (ROT, then HOR, then VER) drives homeHalf() and the mirror targets, so a near wrong twin that
outlives ROT moves half the map off our half. In z3x's losses the opponent took 528 cheese a game from our half by
r300 (141 in wins; scratch pickall.py), 448 of it in the half's outer two depth bands (pickband.py). Of 89 such mines
(100+ taken by r300), we never picked from 26 all game (stolen.py), keepout's (28,47) and (21,47) among them.

Falsifiers, registered before any z5m game:
1. Screen zd192 (vs zd172) on the s6 gates: t <= -1.5, picks/100 per-cell z <= -2, ppr per-round z <= -2, transfer
   per round < 0.97x, any overrun.
2. Mechanism (~/diag26b/sk: keepout, dirtpassageway, FreeTheCheese, Stash, cheesebottles, streetsofnewyork vs araid,
   both seats, z5m and z3x, seed 0, 24 games). On every game-side, z5m's king mask at round 2 must hold the true
   symmetry and must lack the near wrong twin; z3x's mask must still hold that twin (else the switch is inert there).
   z5m must not win fewer of the 12 cells than z3x, and our summed pickups by r300 must not fall. Any one failing
   drops it.
3. Replica: the block rules, plus the transfer floor (0.9x) against z3x's same-set block.
